  "title": "The basics of color contrast ratios",
  "slug": {
    "_type": "slug",
    "current": "importance-color-contrast-ratios-accessible-design-meet-simone-dehel"
  },
  "excerpt": "Hear from Senior UX Designer and accessibility expert, Simone Dehel, to learn how color contrast ratios can make your designs accessible to everyone.",
  "author": {
    "_type": "reference",
    "_ref": "person-wp-7875"
  },
  "categories": [
    {
      "_type": "reference",
      "_ref": "category-wp-63",
      "_key": "cat-63"
    }
  ],
  "publishedAt": "2024-03-28T15:55:51Z",
  "featuredImage": {
    "_type": "figure",
    "image": {
      "_type": "image",
      "_wpSrc": "https://www.o3world.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/03/O3-website-imagery_-Perspectives-37.jpg"
    },
    "alt": "Simone Dehel"
  },
  "body": [
    {
      "_key": "k0008",
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "The world is a vibrant and colorful place, but for some, it can be challenging to navigate. As designers, it is our responsibility to ensure that our work is not only visually appealing but also accessible to all users. One key aspect of creating accessible designs is the appropriate use of color contrast ratios. This article aims to illuminate the benefits of using color contrast ratios and how to effectively apply them in your designs.",
          "_key": "k0009"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "_type": "block",
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "k0010",
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Understanding color contrast ratios",
          "_key": "k0011"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "_type": "block",
      "style": "h3"
    },
    {
      "_key": "k0012",
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Color contrast ratios are the difference in light between the foreground color (the color of the text) and the background color. It’s a numerical value that ranges from 1:1 (no contrast) to 21:1 (maximum contrast). A high contrast ratio makes text more legible and content more distinguishable for users with visual impairments. The Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) recommend a minimum contrast ratio of 4.5:1 for normal text and 3:1 for large text.",
          "_key": "k0013"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "_type": "block",
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "k0014",
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "The role of color contrast ratios",
          "_key": "k0015"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "_type": "block",
      "style": "h3"
    },
    {
      "_key": "k0016",
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Color contrast ratios play a crucial role in creating accessible designs. They ensure that the content is readable by everyone, including those with color vision deficiencies or other visual impairments. High-contrast colors help distinguish text from its background, making the content easier to read and understand. Apart from text, contrast is also required in interactive elements like buttons, forms, and icons, where low contrast can make these components difficult to identify.",
          "_key": "k0017"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "_type": "block",
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "k0018",
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "While most elements need to meet color contrast requirements, ",
          "_key": "k0019"
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "k0000"
          ],
          "text": "WCAG lists a few page elements that do not have a contrast requirement",
          "_key": "k0020"
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": ". These include incidental elements, like text or images of text that are pure decoration, and logotypes, text that is part of a logo or brand name.",
          "_key": "k0021"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "k0000",
          "_type": "link",
          "href": "https://www.w3.org/WAI/WCAG21/Understanding/contrast-minimum"
        }
      ],
      "_type": "block",
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "k0022",
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Integrate accessibility into your process",
          "_key": "k0023"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "_type": "block",
      "style": "h3"
    },
    {
      "_key": "k0024",
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Several tools can assist designers in checking color contrast ratios. Websites like ",
          "_key": "k0025"
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "k0001"
          ],
          "text": "WebAIM",
          "_key": "k0026"
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": " and ",
          "_key": "k0027"
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "k0002"
          ],
          "text": "Colorable",
          "_key": "k0028"
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": " provide free resources to validate if your color combinations adhere to WCAG guidelines.",
          "_key": "k0029"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "k0001",
          "_type": "link",
          "href": "https://webaim.org/resources/contrastchecker/"
        },
        {
          "_key": "k0002",
          "_type": "link",
          "href": "https://colorable.jxnblk.com/"
        }
      ],
      "_type": "block",
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_type": "figure",
      "image": {
        "_type": "image",
        "_wpSrc": "https://www.o3world.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/03/WebAIM.png"
      },
      "alt": "WebAIM",
      "_key": "k0030"
    },
    {
      "_type": "figure",
      "image": {
        "_type": "image",
        "_wpSrc": "https://www.o3world.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/03/Colorable.png"
      },
      "alt": "",
      "_key": "k0031"
    },
    {
      "_key": "k0032",
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Color accessibility with tools like WebAIM and Colorable, ensure your designs meet WCAG guidelines.",
          "_key": "k0033"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "_type": "block",
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "k0034",
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Additionally, Stark’s Accessibility Checker (available as a ",
          "_key": "k0035"
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "k0003"
          ],
          "text": "Chrome extension",
          "_key": "k0036"
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": " and/or ",
          "_key": "k0037"
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "k0004"
          ],
          "text": "Figma plugin",
          "_key": "k0038"
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": ") conveniently checks color combinations against WCAG guidelines and provides recommendations for any color combination that does not pass contrast requirements. Stark’s Accessibility Checker also features a vision simulator that designers can use to see how their designs render for people with vision deficiencies such as color blindness + blurred vision.",
          "_key": "k0039"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "k0003",
          "_type": "link",
          "href": "https://chromewebstore.google.com/detail/stark-accessibility-check/fkfaapnmfippddbeemjjbclenphooipm"
        },
        {
          "_key": "k0004",
          "_type": "link",
          "href": "https://www.figma.com/community/plugin/732603254453395948/stark-contrast-accessibility-tools"
        }
      ],
      "_type": "block",
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_type": "figure",
      "image": {
        "_type": "image",
        "_wpSrc": "https://www.o3world.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/03/Stark_Contrast.png"
      },
      "alt": "Stark contrast example ",
      "_key": "k0040"
    },
    {
      "_type": "figure",
      "image": {
        "_type": "image",
        "_wpSrc": "https://www.o3world.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/03/ab8eb27c-7cb5-4b27-8c72-29caa3c830bc.png"
      },
      "alt": "Stark contrast example ",
      "_key": "k0041"
    },
    {
      "_key": "k0042",
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Seamlessly validate color combinations against WCAG guidelines",
          "_key": "k0043"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "_type": "block",
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
